    in those iterations and may error with find_unused_parameters=False. models/
    racformer_head.py:230, models/racformer_head.py:246
  - High: DN bbox clamp allows exact 0/1 for d/z, but refine_bbox applies
    inverse_sigmoid to d/z, which can yield inf/NaN when values hit 0 or 1.
    Clamp d/z to (EPS, 1-EPS) instead. models/racformer_head.py:393, models/
    racformer_transformer.py:242
  - Medium: has_valid_points uses a tensor in Python boolean context; depending
    on PyTorch/device this can raise a runtime error. Use .sum().item() or
    radar_mask.any() explicitly. models/racformer_head.py:185
  - Medium: polar_radius is passed through the transformer but coordinate
    helpers use default r=65.0 and call sites don’t pass self.polar_radius, so
    any config change is silently ignored and can desync conversions. models/
    bbox/utils.py:82, models/racformer_transformer.py:142
  - Low: safety_anchors assumes 6 clusters (num_query // 6); if num_clusters
    differs, anchor count/pattern will be wrong or mismatched. models/
    rwhi.py:303

  Questions

  - Do you ever run with num_clusters != 6 or polar_radius != 65.0?
  - Are there batches with empty radar points while DDP runs with
    find_unused_parameters=False?

